id: pm-gh1695
title: "GH-1695: accept settings paths and provide bounded config-key recovery"
description: "Canonical intake for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1695. Implement the reported SDK and CLI recovery contract after current-source reproduction, preserving deterministic validation, privacy and no-write refusal behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,config,"gh:1695",sdk
created_at: "2026-11-09T07:32:05.563Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T14:08:48.269Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-09T14:08:46.209Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-09T14:08:46.209Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Accept every supported settings path as an alias in SDK-backed config get/set without bypassing validation; Unknown keys offer at most three nearest legal keys and a working config-list inspection command; Preserve complete legal keys in structured recovery and reject unknown keys without settings writes
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Supported aliases and scalar context leaves use shared descriptor/profile validation with full-depth persistence. Unknown-key recovery retains complete scoped domains. Grouped integer errors disclose decimal syntax and the maximum safe integer.
expected_result: Configuration/profile writes share validation and refusal guidance identifies a legal correction without settings mutation.
actual_result: Both linked configuration/profile commands and all 272 instrumented cohort assertions pass. Grouped scientific/overflow refusals expose grammar/bounds and preserve bytes; the pre-fix overflow assertions failed. Public SDK surface remains unchanged. Final pushed-head hosted quality/native checks and review acceptance remain PENDING.
