comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T07:32:05.563Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus of 3242 items including 2923 closed items and request-specific keyword search reviewed. No matching owner for this GitHub report. Reuse the existing parent capability and preserve closed recovery/configuration lineage."
  "2026-11-09T07:48:19.904Z","harness:codex","Negative-control evidence: new regression assertions ran against unchanged production source before the fix. The focused run failed exactly the settings-path, leading-slash source, matcher-index and strict-close-headline assertions: 4 failures and176 existing passes. Production repair preserves existing validators and sensitive input redaction."
  "2026-11-09T08:30:38.246Z","harness:codex","Completeness review extended the same descriptor-owned configuration surface to the context scalar leaves previously available only through grouped context flags: default depth, activity limit, staleness threshold and the eight existing section toggles. The shared descriptor validators enforce the canonical depth domain, positive safe integers and booleans; real CLI tests check persisted values and byte preservation on invalid depth, zero and unsafe-integer assignments. Existing grouped flags remain supported and help now distinguishes group and leaf writes."
  "2026-11-09T09:53:13.176Z","harness:codex","PR #1696 review remediation: unknown-key inspections retain requested project/global scope; telemetry typo suggestions explicitly identify global-only consent. Dotted context integer leaves reuse the existing complete positive-decimal validator, refusing scientific/hex notation before writes; --default-depth help now includes full. Focused regression and real parser persistence checks are included with the review batch."
  "2026-11-09T10:22:43.102Z","harness:codex","The new direct SDK round-trip regression caught a real persistence mismatch: context.default_depth=full was accepted by the SDK but the settings read validator admitted only brief/standard/deep and returned fallback settings on the next get. The same public CONTEXT_DEPTH_VALUES domain must govern settings reads. This is fixed under the existing configuration owner, with the failing SDK round-trip retained as the negative control."
  "2026-11-09T10:24:42.667Z","harness:codex","Direct SDK regression strengthened the existing nested-leaf owner with context depth/activity/staleness/section round-trips and exact settings-byte preservation for non-decimal/zero refusals. It failed before the full-depth read-validator fix (full resolved as brief), then passed with shared CONTEXT_DEPTH_VALUES. The combined settings/guidance/parser cohort passes 171 tests. Only this configuration owner and pm-gh1693 were reclaimed for these edits."
  "2026-11-09T11:41:56.128Z","harness:codex","Review batch regression control: four intended failures (missing context toggles, incomplete declared recovery aliases, and scientific-number acceptance by profile lint) preceded the shared descriptor fix. All 232 tests across eight files then passed under source instrumentation. Decimal-only context validation is declared internally and reused by profile lint/planning plus grouped/dotted setters; generic integer knobs preserve existing Number syntax. Inventory uses existing summary/min/max fields, avoiding an unnecessary public result-shape extension flagged by the SDK signature gate."
  "2026-11-09T11:55:37.095Z","harness:codex","Final public SDK surface verification reports zero classified changes after keeping numeric-format discovery in the existing metadata fields. Configuration/profile and release/guidance cohorts pass 232 tests; source instrumentation covers the changed strict-integer parser, key recovery and grouped-context parser branches. The optional metadata-only inventory enhancement is separately tracked open/unclaimed in pm-8txeqe."
  "2026-11-09T12:51:18.111Z","harness:codex","Second full-review repair: grouped context integer refusals name the decimal-digits-only grammar. Both grouped numeric options reject scientific notation with that actionable message and preserve settings bytes; project allowed-values regression now excludes both telemetry-tracking and telemetry.enabled. The pre-fix grouped grammar test failed as intended; all 168 focused tests pass."
  "2026-11-09T14:00:02.690Z","harness:codex",Grouped context integer errors now state the shared maximum safe integer as well as decimal-digit syntax. Both grouped numeric options reject overflow with that bound and preserve the settings bytes. The overflow message assertions failed before the wording repair and pass afterward.
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T10:03:47.802Z","harness:codex","Settings paths must resolve through the existing SDK validators and scope rules rather than becoming a parallel write path. Test refusal preservation and consent scope with real settings bytes, including typo suggestions and non-decimal integers."
  "2026-11-09T10:27:53.376Z","harness:codex","CLI subprocess acceptance and direct SDK persistence tests prove different risks: bundled child execution does not instrument the source owner. Source coverage exposed full-depth read rejection and unexercised multi-candidate ranking; meaningful round-trip and ordering cases now cover those contracts before closure."
